275 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 84 0 R
/T (Performance optimization is important in low-code applications because efficiency depends not only on the platform but also on how workflows and scripts are written. In this practical, the Bank Loan Application Form workflow used criteria-based record retrieval with the expression loan_application[ID == input.ID], so that only the required record was retrieved and processed.)
/E (Performance optimization is important in low-code applications because efficiency depends not only on the platform but also on how workflows and scripts are written. In this practical, the Bank Loan Application Form workflow used criteria-based record retrieval with the expression loan_application[ID == input.ID], so that only the required record was retrieved and processed.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
276 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 84 0 R
/T (Targeted record retrieval improves efficiency by avoiding the retrieval of unrelated records and the iteration through them, and efficient workflow design reduces unnecessary processing. Practices such as criteria-based fetching, avoiding unnecessary loops, using built-in operations and keeping workflows simple help applications to handle growing numbers of loan applications. These practices contribute to scalable and maintainable Zoho Creator applications. No benchmark was performed, so the benefits are described in terms of reduced data retrieval and processing and not as measured execution times.)
/E (Targeted record retrieval improves efficiency by avoiding the retrieval of unrelated records and the iteration through them, and efficient workflow design reduces unnecessary processing. Practices such as criteria-based fetching, avoiding unnecessary loops, using built-in operations and keeping workflows simple help applications to handle growing numbers of loan applications. These practices contribute to scalable and maintainable Zoho Creator applications. No benchmark was performed, so the benefits are described in terms of reduced data retrieval and processing and not as measured execution times.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
